# Microservices

## Mục tiêu

Microservices architecture là approach chia nhỏ application thành các services nhỏ, độc lập, mỗi service handle một business capability. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, microservices được sử dụng khi cần scale independently, deploy independently, hoặc use different technology stacks cho different capabilities. Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc apply microservices patterns một cách effective và tránh common pitfalls.

Microservices mang lại nhiều benefits nhưng cũng tăng complexity đáng kể. Rule này giúp identify khi nào nên sử dụng microservices và how to do it right.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Single Responsibility per Service**

Mỗi service handle một business capability. Loose coupling. High cohesion. Clear boundaries. Team ownership.

**2. Smart Endpoints, Dumb Pipes**

Services contain business logic. Pipes are simple transport. Async messaging for decoupling. REST/GraphQL for synchronous.

**3. Decentralized Data Management**

Mỗi service quản lý database riêng. No shared databases. Eventual consistency. Data ownership clear.

**4. Design for Failure**

Services will fail. Circuit breakers. Bulkheads. Retry logic. Graceful degradation.

**5. Infrastructure Automation**

CI/CD for each service. Automated testing. Infrastructure as code. Monitoring và alerting.

**6. Evolutionary Design**

Design for change. Strangler pattern. Feature flags. Incremental migration.

**7. Service Discovery**

Services need to find each other. Service registry. DNS-based discovery. Health checks.

**8. API Gateway**

Single entry point. Request routing. Authentication. Rate limiting. Protocol translation.

**9. Observability**

Distributed tracing. Log aggregation. Metrics collection. Health endpoints.

**10. Team Organization**

Team size: two-pizza rule. Business capability ownership. DevOps culture. Clear ownership.

## Checklist

- [ ] Service boundaries defined
- [ ] API contracts established
- [ ] Service discovery configured
- [ ] Circuit breakers implemented
- [ ] Distributed tracing set up
- [ ] CI/CD pipelines created
- [ ] Monitoring configured
- [ ] Health endpoints implemented
- [ ] Service mesh configured
- [ ] Team ownership assigned

## Anti Pattern

**1. Microservices Monolith**

Distributed monolith. All services tightly coupled. Synchronous everywhere. Shared database. No benefits, all complexity.

**2. Nanoservices**

Too many tiny services. Overhead exceeds benefits. Complexity explosion. Keep services appropriately sized.

**3. Shared Database**

Services share database. Coupling reintroduced. Changes affect multiple services. Separate databases.

**4. Ignoring Fallacies**

Ignoring network issues. Not handling latency. Assuming reliability. Design for failure.

**5. No Observability**

No distributed tracing. Logs not correlated. No metrics. Impossible to debug.

